codex
Read both notes and checked the implementation. No file changes or Convex/EAS commands.

**(1) Corrections**

- **Await native scheduling before recording successful snooze.** Today the intent calls the scheduler, but it launches a detached task with `try?`; the one-second sleep does not guarantee registration. Make that seam `async throws`, preserve guard-first, await cancellation/scheduling, then persist the real armed time and emit. [VRAlarmIntents.swift:607](/C:/Dev/VR/plugins/ios-src/VRAlarmIntents.swift:607), [withAlarmKit.js:512](/C:/Dev/VR/plugins/withAlarmKit.js:512)
- **Apply-then-ack requires N changes too:** replace delete-first draining with `peekEvents()` and `ackEvents(eventIds)`, using durable unique event IDs and serialized append/ack operations. R must make history writes and cancellation replay-safe before acknowledging. [withAlarmKit.js:362](/C:/Dev/VR/plugins/withAlarmKit.js:362), [alarmKit.ts:59](/C:/Dev/VR/lib/alarmKit.ts:59)
- **Expand the native contract:** add occurrence-scoped stop/cancel, and a snapshot-change hint covering countdown, paused and removal—not just alerting/scheduled. Preserve scheduling-failure events. Native `alarmId` must mean UUID; retain `appKey` separately. Existing event `id` means app key. [alarmKit.ts:45](/C:/Dev/VR/lib/alarmKit.ts:45), [withAlarmKit.js:523](/C:/Dev/VR/plugins/withAlarmKit.js:523)
- **Remove day-wide completion from card advancement.** Today one completion skips directly to tomorrow; record and compare `scheduledFor = original occurrenceAt`, including after multiple Laters. [remindersMembership.ts:24](/C:/Dev/VR/lib/remindersMembership.ts:24), [dayOccurrences.ts:197](/C:/Dev/VR/lib/dayOccurrences.ts:197), [index.tsx:1658](/C:/Dev/VR/app/index.tsx:1658)
- **Fallback parity requires additional files:** overlay and alarm-screen handlers independently complete and cap Later. Assign both to R, plus `lib/notificationDecisions.ts`. [AlarmOverlay.tsx:340](/C:/Dev/VR/components/AlarmOverlay.tsx:340), [AlarmOverlay.tsx:384](/C:/Dev/VR/components/AlarmOverlay.tsx:384), [alarm.tsx:214](/C:/Dev/VR/app/alarm.tsx:214), [alarm.tsx:260](/C:/Dev/VR/app/alarm.tsx:260)
- **Define exhaustion explicitly.** A last comeback firing at +15 does not prove ringing ended at +16. Current native configuration has no ring-duration cutoff; JS’s 180-second constant cannot supply one. Do not mark Missed while a current snapshot still says alerting. [withAlarmKit.js:446](/C:/Dev/VR/plugins/withAlarmKit.js:446), [alarmKit.ts:66](/C:/Dev/VR/lib/alarmKit.ts:66)
- **Lifecycle needs ordering and chain identity:** add `chainId`, `chainStartedAt`, `lastFireAt`, `lastEventAt`, `lastEventId`; propagate chain identity through native metadata/events. Ignore stale generations; Done must not be resurrected by elapsed-time inference. Prune resolved records after two days, retaining unresolved rings/snoozes.
- **Use one serialized reconciliation coordinator**, called by tick, foreground and native hints; publish a reactive lifecycle snapshot after reconciliation. Separate storage reads can reproduce today’s refresh race. [index.tsx:350](/C:/Dev/VR/app/index.tsx:350), [_layout.tsx:109](/C:/Dev/VR/app/_layout.tsx:109)

**(2) Q1–Q5**

- **Q1:** Yes, this is a viable background-intent path; this checkout already attempts follow-up scheduling from `perform()` and cancels siblings from Stop. It is **not currently reliable by construction**, because registration errors disappear in the detached task. Retain the concrete alarm UUID and stable occurrence metadata in each newly configured intent. [VRAlarmIntents.swift:567](/C:/Dev/VR/plugins/ios-src/VRAlarmIntents.swift:567), [VRAlarmIntents.swift:685](/C:/Dev/VR/plugins/ios-src/VRAlarmIntents.swift:685), [withAlarmKit.js:449](/C:/Dev/VR/plugins/withAlarmKit.js:449)
